    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "I don't really want anything done about this issue - it's just recording what I've found out so far.\n\nOur Python 3.14 windows on ARM CI runs are currently failing. It times out when linking refnanny. @ksunden kindly confirmed that this happens on real hardware and not just Github Actions (tagging just to give credit.... I definitely don't want to drag you into this further). He also confirmed that it also happens on Python 3.13, and doesn't seem to be bisectable to a specific Cython version (which suggests to me that it might started recently due to a setuptools update changing build flags or something similar).\n\nThis doesn't affect our Windows on ARM wheels (possibly because they're Limited API, or possibly because cibuildwheel uses different default flags, or possibly something else; I haven't investigated) but does affect our testing of the platform.\n\nI've:\n* [Reported the bug to Microsoft](https://developercommunity.microsoft.com/t/MSVC-ARM64-linkexe-hangs-building-Cytho/11167595)\n* [Whinged on discuss.python.org](https://discuss.python.org/t/python-on-windows-arm64/104524/29) - this isn't really to achieve anything except make me feel better.\n\nIf we did want to try to make the CI green I think we could disable the Cython build and turn off refnanny for this platform. That's the limit of what we should do to work around a Microsoft bug and even then I'm not sure we should do that because this kind of \"fix\" just accumulates as junk in ci-run.sh.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Microsoft say that they've fixed the issue so presumably it'll be in the next visual studio update (although I don't know when that'll be or how long it'll take to make it into the arm runners). But to me that points to \"do nothing and wait\" as the best option",
